tickets.body:
**Change**
- **Migration V10** in `src/core/db/migrations.ts`; bump `SCHEMA_VERSION`.
  - `transfers` (primary key epic_id): target 'linear', status queued|in_progress|verified|canceled, revision_id, packet_hash, packet_json, project_id, project_url, last_mismatches_json, queued_by, queued_at, started_at, updated_at, session_id.
  - `transfer_items`: epic_id, ref, kind project|milestone|issue|relation, linear_id, identifier, url, recorded_at; primary key (epic_id, ref).
- **Capabilities.** `transfer.queue` is human-only (add it to `HUMAN_ONLY_CAPABILITIES`; the desktop holds it). `epic.transfer` goes to the orchestrator and the desktop. Update the role and human-only lists that `src/core/authz.test.ts` and `src/core/commands/capabilities.test.ts` pin.
- **Services** in `src/core/services/transfers.ts`:
  - `queueTransfer(ctx, { epicId })` (transfer.queue): build the packet from the current saved revision and store it with its hash. Refusals:
    - a completed epic: `completed_epic`;
    - an active run: `active_run_exists`;
    - no saved revision: `invalid_plan`;
    - an unsaved draft change: `conflict`, as `changedDraftRevision` does;
    - an open transfer: `conflict`.
  - `cancelTransfer(ctx, { epicId })` (transfer.queue): mark it canceled and clear its items. The Linear items stay; a later transfer adopts them by marker.
  - `startTransfer(ctx, { epicId })` (epic.transfer): move a queued transfer to in_progress, or resume an in_progress one. Return `{ packet, recorded, next }` from the stored packet. Without an open transfer it fails: "The person has not authorized a transfer of this epic."
  - `recordTransferItem(ctx, { epicId, ref, linearId, identifier?, url? })` (epic.transfer) works only while in_progress. The ref must be in the packet. Re-recording the same values is a no-op. A different linearId for a recorded ref is a `conflict` unless `replace: true`.
  - `getTransfer(ctx, { epicId })` (read) returns the status (`not_started` when none exists), the packet (stored, or built from the current saved revision when none exists), the recorded items, `lastMismatches` and `next` (the unrecorded refs in packet order). It never writes.
- Each mutation appends its event in the same transaction: `transfer.queued`, `transfer.canceled`, `transfer.started` or `transfer.item_recorded`.
- Add `DELETE FROM transfer_items` and `DELETE FROM transfers` to `DELETE_STATEMENTS` (`src/core/services/epicDeletion.ts`), before `epics`.

**Tests** (write and run in this ticket):
- `src/core/services/transfers.test.ts`:
  - each refusal with its code;
  - start without a queued transfer fails;
  - resume returns the stored packet, and `next` skips what was recorded;
  - a changed linearId conflicts, and succeeds with replace;
  - cancel clears the items;
  - the packet stays fixed when a ticket status changes after queuing.
- `authz.test.ts` and `capabilities.test.ts`: transfer.queue is human-only, and epic.transfer is held by the orchestrator and the desktop.
- The migrations test: V10 upgrades a V9 database.
- `src/core/commands/deletion.test.ts`: deleting an epic with a transfer succeeds.

**Checks:** typecheck; `npx oxlint` on the files you touched; the tests listed above plus the existing tests of the files you touched. Do not run the full suite, coverage, whole-tree lint, a build (unless a criterion needs one) or Fireguard.

**Change**
Add `submitTransferReadback(ctx, { epicId, readback, final })` in `src/core/services/transfers.ts` (capability epic.transfer, while in_progress).

**Read-back shape.** Parts accumulate until `final: true`, so a large project can be sent in pages. It holds:
- the project: `{ linearId, url, name, summary, content }`;
- the milestones: `{ linearId, name, description }`;
- the issues: `{ linearId, identifier, milestoneId, title, description, priority, labels, stateType, sortOrder? }`;
- the relations: `{ kind, fromId, toId }`.

**Comparison** against the stored packet and the recorded mapping, on the final part. A mismatch is `{ ref, key?, field, expected, actual }`.
- Every packet ref is recorded and present in the read-back.
- The project name matches, and the marker is in its summary.
- Milestone names match, in position order.
- Each issue:
  - is in its milestone;
  - has its title and priority;
  - has its labels, compared as a case-insensitive set;
  - has a description containing its checklist lines, back-link and marker;
  - has a completed stateType for a completed ticket, and neither completed nor canceled for any other.
- The blocks and related relations match as sets.
- `unexpected`: a read-back issue or milestone whose id is not recorded.
- `duplicate`: two items with the same marker.
- `team`: identifiers with different team keys.

**Warnings**, not mismatches:
- `identifier_order`: identifier numbers not rising in position;
- `sort_order_unreported`, or `sort_order` when the reported sortOrder does not rise.

**No mismatch: one transaction.**
- Recheck: no active run, the saved revision is still the transfer's, and no unsaved draft change.
- Add the comment through `addComment` (nested transactions are supported) before the status changes. It holds the Linear project link and the counts.
- Set the epic completed (`completed_at`, revision + 1). Its outcome is `{ summary: 'Transferred to Linear: <url>', successCriteria: [], recordedAt, runId: null, transfer: { target: 'linear', projectUrl, revisionId, packetHash, items: [{ key, identifier, url }] } }`.
- Mark the transfer verified and append `epic.transferred`; the epic_state and comment exports follow.

**Any mismatch:** store the mismatches in `last_mismatches_json`, append `transfer.readback_rejected` and return them. The epic stays open.

**Outcome type and record.** `EpicOutcome` (`src/shared/domain/views.ts`) gains an optional `transfer`. The strict `epicOutcome` in `src/core/repo/portable.ts` accepts it as `.optional()`, with no default, so an outcome without it re-exports byte for byte. Older app versions show such an epic as rejected until they update.

**Completion wording.** Update `COMPLETION_RULE` (`src/core/services/epics.ts:99`) and its pin at `epics.test.ts:437`, the `set_epic_status` description (`src/core/commands/authoring.ts`) and `skills/sprint-reporter.md`. Each should read: an epic completes when its final checkpoint advances, or when a verified Linear transfer completes it.

**Tests** (write and run in this ticket):
- In `transfers.test.ts`:
  - one mismatch test per field, plus unexpected, duplicate and team;
  - the warnings do not block;
  - paged parts accumulate;
  - a full match completes the epic with the outcome, the comment and the event;
  - a failure injected inside the transaction leaves the epic open;
  - after completion, start_run, update_plan_draft and queueTransfer are refused.
- A 1,000-ticket fixture completes.
- A portable or importer test: outcome.transfer round-trips, and an outcome without it re-exports unchanged.

**Checks:** typecheck; `npx oxlint` on the files you touched; the tests listed above plus the existing tests of the files you touched. Do not run the full suite, coverage, whole-tree lint, a build (unless a criterion needs one) or Fireguard.

**Change**
- New `docs/runbooks/linear-transfer.md`, covering:
  - the prerequisites: a saved plan, no active run, and an agent with Linear's MCP server set up (the commands per CLI);
  - authorization in the app, and Linear sign-in and team choice;
  - the mapping table (epic, sprint, ticket, acceptance node, edges, related links, criteria, priority, tags, state, marker);
  - the order rules, verification with its mismatches and warnings, resume, cancel and the run/Save lock;
  - what completion records;
  - the limits: one-time, no sync, no estimates, Linear only.
  Include both starts: the workspace button, and Copy prompt or `dm transfer linear` with an external agent.
- Link it from `README.md` (features) and `docs/runbooks/mcp-setup.md`.
- Add a decision note to `docs/architecture.md`: the agent-executed transfer, the human authorization, DM's read-back check and its trust limit.

**Tests** (write and run in this ticket)
- None: documentation. Check that every relative link in the changed docs resolves.

**Checks:** a link check by hand or script; no code checks are needed.
